+        // Tiles advance by `stride` in screen space, but the element's
+        // transform also scales the tile itself, so the untransformed stride is
+        // the wrong spacing to cull (or step) with: a scaled-down box loses the
+        // tiles past the first `1/scale` of the viewport. When the transform is
+        // an axis-aligned positive scale, scale the stride too. A rotation,
+        // skew or flip has no per-axis stride, so keep every tile instead of
+        // culling with a spacing the tiling does not use.
+        let [a, b, c, d, ..] = base_transform.as_coeffs();
